# Files `scripts/alert-delivery.mjs` writes at bring-up. None of them are source:
# each is rendered from configuration for the lifetime of one verification run and
# removed again in the script's `finally`.
#
# `deploy/staging/.gitignore` already covers `metrics-token` for the same reason;
# these two are here rather than there so that everything generated into this
# directory is declared in the directory it appears in.

# Rendered from alertmanager.template.yml. It is the file Alertmanager actually
# loads, and it names this deployment's real paging destinations — which is
# precisely why it must not be committed: a tracked copy is one merge away from
# pointing somebody else's staging run at your on-call phone.
alertmanager.yml

# The SMTP submission password, written from PRL_ALERT_SMTP_PASSWORD at mode 0600
# and mounted read-only into the alertmanager container. Empty when no
# `PRL_ALERT_SMTP_USERNAME` is configured, and written anyway so that the bind
# mount resolves against a FILE — Docker answers a missing bind-mount source by
# creating a directory, and Alertmanager reports that as an unreadable password
# rather than as a missing file.
smtp-password
